gaussRing -- ring of gaussian correlations on n random variables
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        gaussRing n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of random variables
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing (missing documentation) => ..., default value QQ, a
        coefficient field or ring
      * Variable (missing documentation) => ..., default value "s", a symbol,
        the variables in the ring will be s_(1,1),...
  * Outputs:
      * a ring with indeterminates s_(i,j), 1 <= i <= j <= n, a *note ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,

Description
===========

The routines gaussMinors (missing documentation), *note gaussIdeal:
gaussIdeal,, gaussTrekIdeal (missing documentation) all require that the ring
be created by this function.


+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = gaussRing 5;                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : gens R                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   ,|
|       1,1   1,2   1,3   1,4   1,5   2,2   2,3   2,4   2,5   3,3   3,4   3,5 |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     s   , s   , s   }                                                       |
|      4,4   4,5   5,5                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : genericSymmetricMatrix(R,5)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | s_(1,1) s_(1,2) s_(1,3) s_(1,4) s_(1,5) |                             |
|     | s_(1,2) s_(2,2) s_(2,3) s_(2,4) s_(2,5) |                             |
|     | s_(1,3) s_(2,3) s_(3,3) s_(3,4) s_(3,5) |                             |
|     | s_(1,4) s_(2,4) s_(3,4) s_(4,4) s_(4,5) |                             |
|     | s_(1,5) s_(2,5) s_(3,5) s_(4,5) s_(5,5) |                             |
|                                                                             |
|             5      5                                                        |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

